"(tcp or udp or sctp) and ((src host 1.1.1.1 and dst host 8.8.8.8) or (src host 1:2:3:4:5:6:7:8 and dst host 4:4:4:4:4:4:4:4)) and src port 8080 and dst port 4242"

NOTE: BPF supports (limited) loops. The tcpdump `protochain` command for IPv6 enables filtering protocol after all the IPv6 headers have been traversed; this is important for full coverage. It doesn't seem to support *all* IPv6 headers though; notably, the Mobility Header and both Destination Options header numbers are missing (see https://www.cisco.com/en/US/technologies/tk648/tk872/technologies_white_paper0900aecd8054d37d.html).


Special protocols: TCP, UDP, DCCP, SCTP, UDP-Lite (6, 17, 33, 132, 136)

1. IPv4 || IPv6 || Any

2. User-specified protocol || Portful protocol || Any

3. 



[23] -> #poff + 11

(000) ld       proto
(001) jeq      #0x800           jt 2	jf ipv6     ; if IPv6-only, change to jt ipv6
(002) ld       poff
(003) add      #0x9                          ; Get the protocol index
(004) tax
(005) ldh      %x
(006) jeq      #0x6             jt 11	jf 4 ; if specific proto, change to #0x<proto> and jf fail; if any, change to jf 11
(007) jeq      #0x11            jt 11   jf 5
(008) jeq      #0x21            jt 11	jf 6 
(009) jeq      #0x84            jt 11	jf 7 
(010) jeq      #0x88            jt 11   jf fail

Address cases:
a. src=A && dst=B (local: Some, remote: Some, direction: Outgoing || Incoming)
b. (src=A && dst=B) || (src=B && dst=A) (local: Some, remote: Some, direction: Bidirectional)
c. src=A || dst=A (local: Some, remote: None, direction: Bidirectional) || (local: None, remote: Some, direction: Bidirectional)
d. src=A (local: Some, remote: None, direction: Outgoing) || (local: None, remote: Some, direction: Incoming)
e. dst=A (local: None, remote: Some, direction: Outgoing) || (local: Some, remote: None, direction: Incoming)
f. <null> (local: None, remote: None, direction: any)

; Decision tree: (f. is an immediate Success)
; 1. src=A ? 2 : 3          // success leaf: c, d | fail leaf: a
; 2. dst=B ? Success : Fail // success leaf: a, b | fail leaf: a, b
; 3. dst=A ? 4 : Fail       // success leaf: c, e | fail leaf: c, e
; 4. src=B ? Success : Fail // success leaf: b    | fail leaf: b


; Check if src=A
(011) ld       [x + 3]
(012) jeq      #0x10101010      jt 13   jf 15
(013) ld       [x + 7]
(014) jeq      #0x80808080      jt 19   jf fail
(015) ld       [x + 7]
(016) jeq      #0x10101010      jt 17   jf fail
(017) ld       [x + 3]
(018) jeq      #0x80808080      jt 19   jf fail
; src/dst addresses matched in some way; now check port numbers
(019) ld 


(013) jeq      #0x80808080      jt 14   jf fail ; replace with `remote` (depending on direction)
; AND path
(014) ld       [x + 7]
(015) jeq      #0x80808080      jt 20   jf 16 ; if only one direction, jf fail; replace with `remote` (depending on direction)
(016) jeq      #0x10101010      jt 20   jf fail
; OR path--useed only when local is Some, remote is None and 
(017) ld       [x + 7]
(018) jeq      #0x80808080      jt 17   jf 16 ; if only one direction, jf fail; replace with `remote` (depending on direction)
(019) jeq      #0x10101010      jt 17   jf fail



